{"schema":"ntui-app-v1","generatedUtc":"2026-10-30T02:47:51.003Z","dataThrough":"2026-10-29","thesis":"Are the native tokens (CC, LINK, QNT) actually used by the systems and companies making tokenization claims?","verdicts":[{"token":"CC","verdict":"INCONCLUSIVE","label":"MIXED","plain":"Real demand shows up, but not enough for a clear yes or no.","color":"amber","reason":"Coverage, trend or completeness does not meet a decisive rule.","supporting":[],"contradicting":["30d burn coverage 0.671 (burned / minted).","90d burn trend FLAT (ratio 0.94)."],"gaps":["Source is Lighthouse (lighthouse.xyz), a third-party ETL of Canton Scan; official Scan returns 403 to non-validator IPs.","Dedicated synchronizers are NOT_OBSERVABLE in Scan (structural; CIP-0129 is APPROVED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED).","Holding-fee expiry burns (Amulet_Expire*) are counted but their amount is NOT_OBSERVABLE.","Minted excludes dev-fund mint (about 5% of issuance; not served per day), so coverage is overstated by up to ~5%.","2 day(s) of burns are LOWER_BOUND (top-50 cap); NOT_SUPPORTED is blocked."]},{"token":"LINK","verdict":"NOT_SUPPORTED","label":"NO","plain":"Measured demand for the token is not keeping up with new supply or with network use.","color":"red","reason":"CCIP mainnet activity rose (x1.64) while measured LINK demand did not keep pace: 90d Reserve inflow 1,264,099 LINK is under 10% of the 18,750,000 LINK released. Fee token measured for messages sent from Ethereum only: 0.7% (130 of 17,512) paid the fee in LINK over 30 day(s); other source chains are NOT_OBSERVABLE.","supporting":["30d Reserve inflow 427,578 LINK."],"contradicting":["0.7% of CCIP messages sent from Ethereum paid the fee in LINK (130 of 17,512, 30 day(s)); the rest paid in ETH or other tokens.","Reserve inflows FLAT over 90d (ratio 0.94).","30d inflow 427,578 vs 30d LINK released 18,750,000 from official non-circulating wallets.","CCIP mainnet activity RISING (ratio 1.64) - usage growth to compare against inflows."],"gaps":["CCIP fee token is measured only for messages sent from Ethereum; other source chains are NOT_OBSERVABLE. LINK is not required to pay CCIP fees.","Reserve inflows do not show which customer or product the converted revenue came from."]},{"token":"QNT","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT_DATA","label":"NOT ENOUGH DATA","plain":"The data needed to judge is missing or not public yet.","color":"gray","reason":"No public source shows QNT being spent or locked to use the Quant network (licence fees, Fusion gas, staking).","supporting":[],"contradicting":["An Overledger licence costs £100/yr, about 0.75 QNT today; even 1,000 licences would need about 748 QNT a year (0.005% of the 14,612,493 QNT supply).","unknown QNT transfers on Ethereum over 4 day(s); this is mostly exchange and DEX trading, not network usage."],"gaps":["Licence fees paid in QNT are NOT_OBSERVABLE: Quant has not published the treasury contract address.","Fusion gas paid in QNT is NOT_OBSERVABLE: no public Fusion mainnet explorer or Ethereum deposit contract (only Fusion Rollup Testnet is readable via the Overledger API).","QNT staking is NOT_AVAILABLE (not live publicly).","On-chain totalSupply 45,467,000 minus 9,550,893 burned into the token contract does not equal the official 14,612,493; the difference is not explained in the sources checked."]}],"questions":[{"id":"cc_burn","token":"CC","question":"Is Canton Coin being used up as fast as new coins are created?","answer":"For every 100 new CC created in the last 30 days, about 67 were burned (used up paying for the network). Creation is ahead of burning, so supply is still growing.","number":67,"unit":"burned per 100 created"},{"id":"cc_who","token":"CC","question":"Who is actually burning Canton Coin?","answer":"Three accounts (temple-mainnet-1, kora-mainNetValidator-1, cantor8-digik-1) did 79.3% of all burning. Claimed institutions found burning: DTCC-Validator-1 (dtcc) (0.2%).","number":79.3,"unit":"% of burn by top 3"},{"id":"cc_rewards","token":"CC","question":"Is the burning paid for by the network's own rewards?","answer":"0.1% of the burning comes from accounts whose app rewards fully cover what they burn (burning that pays for itself). 32.4% comes from accounts whose rewards cover less than half, so they mostly pay out of pocket.","number":0.1,"unit":"% reward-funded"},{"id":"link_reserve","token":"LINK","question":"Is Chainlink revenue buying LINK faster than new LINK is released?","answer":"For every 100 LINK released from Chainlink's locked supply in the last 90 days, about 6.7 went into the Chainlink Reserve. Reserve inflows are flat.","number":6.7,"unit":"into Reserve per 100 released"},{"id":"link_usage","token":"LINK","question":"Is the Chainlink network (CCIP) being used more?","answer":"Yes: cross-chain messages were 64% higher in the second half of the last 90 days than the first. 65,725 messages across all chains in the last 30 days. Reserve buying is flat over the same 90 days; that gap is what this page tracks.","number":64,"unit":"% usage growth"},{"id":"link_fees","token":"LINK","question":"When people use Chainlink CCIP, do they pay the fee in LINK?","answer":"Mostly no. Of 17,512 cross-chain messages sent from Ethereum over 30 days, 130 (0.7%) paid in LINK. The rest paid in ETH or other tokens, which Chainlink converts to LINK later (that shows up as Reserve buys).","number":0.7,"unit":"% of fees paid in LINK"},{"id":"qnt_usage","token":"QNT","question":"Is the Quant network using up QNT?","answer":"Cannot tell yet. QNT is supposed to be spent on Overledger licences and on Fusion gas, but Quant has not published the addresses where that QNT goes, and Fusion has no public explorer. For scale: a licence is £100 a year, about 0.75 QNT today, so 1,000 licences would use about 748 QNT a year out of 14,612,493.","number":null,"unit":"not observable"}],"blindSpots":["Private Canton networks (where most bank tokenization runs) burn no CC today, so their use cannot show up here. CIP-0129 (approved Oct 21, 2026; expected around Q1 2027) would change that.","Account names are chosen by their operators. A bank running through a vendor's node shows the vendor's name.","The CCIP fee token is read only for messages sent from Ethereum, the busiest source chain. Fees paid on other chains are not counted yet.","Quant: licence fees and Fusion gas paid in QNT happen where no public record exists yet. QNT transfers on Ethereum are mostly trading.","Canton numbers come from Lighthouse, a third-party copy of the official Canton data (the official servers only answer approved validators)."],"numbers":{"cc":{"minted30":643109329,"burned30":431743806,"coverage30":0.6713381169681083,"burnTrend90":"FLAT","burnTrendRatio":0.9398212216307997,"source":"OK_SECONDARY"},"link":{"inflow30":427578,"released30":18750000,"inflow90":1264099,"released90":18750000,"inflowTrend":"FLAT","ccip30":65725,"ccipTrendRatio":1.6374575413745753,"reserveBalance":6475076,"feeDays30":30,"feeMsgs30":17512,"feeLink30":130,"feeLinkShare30":0.007423481041571494},"qnt":{"transfers30":null,"transferDays30":4,"holders":194254,"holderChange30":null,"officialSupply":14612493,"onchainSupply":45467000,"heldByContract":9550893,"licenseGbp":100,"licenseQnt":0.7475,"price":178.16}},"who":{"end":"2026-10-29","top3":0.793353475171301,"watch":0.0018234685174040005,"rewardFunded":0.0010711167629361834,"netPayer":0.3240695683716201,"matches":["DTCC-Validator-1 (dtcc)"],"rows":[{"name":"temple-mainnet-1","burned":197222703,"share":0.4568,"rewards":137650987,"role":"PARTLY_FUNDED","match":""},{"name":"kora-mainNetValidator-1","burned":102336401,"share":0.237,"rewards":0,"role":"NET_PAYER","match":""},{"name":"cantor8-digik-1","burned":42966344,"share":0.0995,"rewards":25168633,"role":"PARTLY_FUNDED","match":""},{"name":"ObsidianSystems-validator-2","burned":29824239,"share":0.0691,"rewards":0,"role":"NET_PAYER","match":""},{"name":"pixelplex-mainnet-3","burned":21979958,"share":0.0509,"rewards":12865899,"role":"PARTLY_FUNDED","match"